# membank-resolved.khdl — membank with seed queries the swarm has already
# answered, so every leaf resolves to a real discovered primitive.
#
# First lab run (2026-08-02, 3,216-primitive registry snapshot) surfaced a
# genuine H3 finding: this resolved bank UNDERPERFORMED the unresolved
# membank.khdl (26% vs 47% persistence of crystallized structures) —
# because resolution also chooses the field material. The resolved seeds
# were metamaterial-discovered, and metamaterial dissipates hard under
# deep dreams, while membank's unresolved fallback ran in ideal_resonator
# and GAINED energy through consolidation (423 -> 468). Architecture
# quality is coupled to medium choice; surfacing that is the point.
#
# Run it (isolated lab — see README "Running grown architectures"):
#   kannaka-hdl grow examples/membank-resolved.khdl --emit crystal -o bank.crystal
#   KANNAKA_CRYSTAL_DATA_DIR=/tmp/bank-lab kannaka-crystal run bank.crystal

cell MemoryBank(n) {
    when n > 1  => split MemoryBank(n / 2), MemoryBank(n / 2) bridge "Harmonic Bridge"
    when always => base "Standing Echo" min_persistence 0.5
}

grow MemoryBank(8)
